{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++11 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++11 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nusing ll = long long;\nusing ull = unsigned long long;\nusing pii = pair<int, int>;\nusing pll = pair<ll, ll>;\n\nconst int MOD = 1000000007;\n\nint n, S, cnt[250], id[250];\nint f[10][250];\nvector<int> vec[10];\nunordered_map<ull, int> cache;\n\nint mod_exp(int base, int exp) {\n    int result = 1;\n    base %= MOD;\n    while (exp > 0) {\n        if (exp & 1) {\n            result = (1LL * result * base) % MOD;\n        }\n        base = (1LL * base * base) % MOD;\n        exp >>= 1;\n    }\n    return result;\n}\n\nint solve(int pos, ull state) {\n    if (state == 0) return 0;\n    if (pos == n) return 1;\n    \n    ull key = (static_cast<ull>(pos) << 32) | state;\n    if (cache.find(key) != cache.end()) return cache[key];\n    \n    ++S;\n    int total = 0;\n    \n    for (int mask = 1; mask < (1 << n); ++mask) {\n        ull next_state = 0;\n        for (int idx = 0; idx < vec[pos].size(); ++idx) {\n            if (!(state & (1ULL << idx))) continue;\n            int prev = vec[pos][idx];\n            for (int bit = 0; bit < n; ++bit) {\n                if ((mask & (1 << bit)) && !(prev & (1 << bit))) {\n                    next_state |= 1ULL << id[prev | (1 << bit)];\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        total = (total + 1LL * f[pos][mask] * solve(pos + 1, next_state)) % MOD;\n    }\n    \n    return cache[key] = total;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ios_base::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n    \n    cin >> n;\n    int inv100 = mod_exp(100, MOD - 2);\n    \n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        f[i][0] = 1;\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n            int P;\n            cin >> P;\n            int p1 = (1LL * P * inv100) % MOD;\n            int p0 = (1 + MOD - p1) % MOD;\n            for (int k = 0; k < (1 << j); ++k) {\n                f[i][k | (1 << j)] = (1LL * f[i][k] * p1) % MOD;\n                f[i][k] = (1LL * f[i][k] * p0) % MOD;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    \n    for (int i = 0; i < (1 << n); ++i) {\n        cnt[i] = __builtin_popcount(i);\n    }\n    \n    for (int i = 0; i < (1 << n); ++i) {\n        vec[cnt[i]].push_back(i);\n        id[i] = vec[cnt[i]].size() - 1;\n    }\n    \n    cout << solve(0, 1) << '\\n';\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\nfrom collections import defaultdict\n\nMOD = 1000000007\n\ndef mod_exp(base, exp):\n    result = 1\n    base %= MOD\n    while exp > 0:\n        if exp & 1:\n            result = (result * base) % MOD\n        base = (base * base) % MOD\n        exp >>= 1\n    return result\n\ndef solve(pos, state, n, f, vec, id_map, cache):\n    if state == 0:\n        return 0\n    if pos == n:\n        return 1\n    \n    key = (pos << 32) | state\n    if key in cache:\n        return cache[key]\n    \n    total = 0\n    for mask in range(1, 1 << n):\n        next_state = 0\n        for idx in range(len(vec[pos])):\n            if not (state & (1 << idx)):\n                continue\n            prev = vec[pos][idx]\n            for bit in range(n):\n                if (mask & (1 << bit)) and not (prev & (1 << bit)):\n                    next_state |= 1 << id_map[prev | (1 << bit)]\n        total = (total + f[pos][mask] * solve(pos + 1, next_state, n, f, vec, id_map, cache)) % MOD\n    \n    cache[key] = total\n    return total\n\ndef main():\n    input = sys.stdin.read\n    data = input().split()\n    \n    n = int(data[0])\n    inv100 = mod_exp(100, MOD - 2)\n    \n    f = [[0] * (1 << n) for _ in range(n)]\n    index = 1\n    \n    for i in range(n):\n        f[i][0] = 1\n        for j in range(n):\n            P = int(data[index])\n            index += 1\n            p1 = (P * inv100) % MOD\n            p0 = (1 + MOD - p1) % MOD\n            for k in range(1 << j):\n                f[i][k | (1 << j)] = (f[i][k] * p1) % MOD\n                f[i][k] = (f[i][k] * p0) % MOD\n    \n    cnt = [0] * (1 << n)\n    for i in range(1 << n):\n        cnt[i] = bin(i).count('1')\n    \n    vec = [[] for _ in range(n + 1)]\n    id_map = [0] * (1 << n)\n    \n    for i in range(1 << n):\n        vec[cnt[i]].append(i)\n        id_map[i] = len(vec[cnt[i]]) - 1\n    \n    cache = {}\n    result = solve(0, 1, n, f, vec, id_map, cache)\n    print(result)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00017248096992261708, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.00045622908510267735, -0.00027581225731410086, -0.0004970983718521893, -0.07400031387805939, -0.3297918438911438, -3.576278118089249e-07, -5.483612312673358e-06, -0.007620786316692829, -0.16123279929161072, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -6.198863957251888e-06, -0.0005534547381103039, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -2.0265558760002023e-06, -1.0013530300057027e-05, -0.0007493072189390659, -6.747018051100895